# Documentation

All project documentation lives in `hospitia-master/docs/` (MkDocs Material). READMEs in `hospitia-frontend` and `hospitia-backend` are short stubs: purpose, port, commands and links only.

- Put each page in the Diátaxis section that matches its job: `tutorials/`, `guides/`, `reference/`, `architecture/` or `about/`, `standards/`, `getting-started/`, `backend/`, `frontend/`, `operations/`, `adr/`.
- New page: kebab-case file name, add it to `nav` in `mkdocs.yml`, link it from the section's `index.md`.
- One H1, then a one or two sentence intro. Facts only from the code; unknown intent becomes a `!!! note "TODO"` admonition, never a guess. Don't duplicate content; link to the owning page.
- Links between docs pages are relative `.md` links; links to root files or other repositories are absolute GitHub URLs. `CHANGELOG.md` must contain only absolute links (it's included in the site).
- Never put secrets, tokens, real passwords or `.env` values in docs; document settings by name and purpose. Local-development credentials only on local-development pages, labelled.
- Never hand-edit `docs/reference/api/*.openapi.json`; run `bash scripts/export_openapi.sh`.
- Changelog: add entries under `[Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md`, grouped by Added/Changed/Deprecated/Removed/Fixed/Security, starting with `[frontend]`, `[backend:<service>]`, `[infra]` or `[docs]` and ending with a PR or commit reference.
- Run `bash scripts/check_docs.sh` before finishing (strict build plus agent rule and skill drift checks).

Details: `docs/standards/documentation.md`.
